---
title: Proposed recovery — engine confirmation and retained uncertainty
---
flowchart TB
  accTitle: Proposed operator recovery for native CDDA
  accDescr: The operator first pauses new gameplay. A request at a supported activity poll opens the engine confirmation, which the operator answers against its exact frame. A raw debug prompt can instead receive one explicitly requested Space. Unsupported or uncertain outcomes retain native fallback. Every path requires observation and reconciliation, and only a normal-play boundary permits explicit resume. No path automatically resumes gameplay or proves task success.
  P["Operator pauses\nRevoke new gameplay"]
  A["Request activity interruption\nAt supported engine poll"]
  Q["CDDA confirmation\nOperator answers exact prompt"]
  D["Visible debug prompt\nOperator requests one Space"]
  U["Unsupported or unknown\nKeep paused; native fallback"]
  O["Observe and reconcile\nPreserve original action outcome"]
  R["Normal play verified\nOperator may explicitly resume"]
  P -->|Activity still running| A
  A -->|Engine asks| Q
  A -->|No eligible boundary or deadline| U
  P -->|Specific error frame| D
  Q -->|YES or NO delivered| O
  D -->|Dismissal delivered| O
  Q -->|Uncertain result| U
  D -->|Uncertain result| U
  U -->|Native recovery when needed| O
  O -->|Still blocked or unresolved| U
  O -->|Fresh eligible boundary| R
